  "id": "ciliary-processes",
  "term": "ciliary processes",
  "definition": "Ciliary processes are structures in the epithelial part of the ciliary body, a ring of tissue that runs from the scleral spur to the ora serrata of the retina. The ciliary body has two parts: a uveal portion, which contains the ciliary muscle, and an epithelial portion, which contains the ciliary processes.",
